WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.680
At long last, fans of DC Comics once again&nbsp;
have a reason to buy a ticket at their local&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:10.880
movie theater. To kick off their packed DC&nbsp;
slate for 2022, Warner Bros. released "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:16.800
Batman" on March 4th, courtesy of director Matt&nbsp;
Reeves. In this non-DC Extended Universe flick,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:21.920
we see the titular Dark Knight — played by Robert&nbsp;
Pattinson — in the midst of his second year as an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:26.800
armored vigilante. However, he's not up against&nbsp;
petty thieves and robbers this time around.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:32.000
Rather, he has to contend with an intelligent&nbsp;
and dangerous entity known as the Riddler.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.080
Batfans beware: Spoilers ahead!

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:40.400
Throughout "The Batman," Edward "Riddler" Nashton&nbsp;
turns the entire city of Gotham on its head.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:45.680
Instead of going on a mindless murder spree, he&nbsp;
meticulously goes after several individuals in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:50.000
positions of power, killing them and publicly&nbsp;
dragging their names through the mud. All the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:55.760
while, he leaves a series of codes, ciphers, and&nbsp;
riddles to keep the Gotham City Police Department&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:00.960
and Batman on their toes. Thankfully, they&nbsp;
eventually end Riddler's sadistic revenge game and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:06.320
stick him in Arkham State Hospital, but not before&nbsp;
the final stage of his master plan could begin.

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:11.680
Riddler acted alone for most of "The Batman"&nbsp;
until the tail end of the film. His numerous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:15.920
followers from dark corners of the internet&nbsp;
stepped out of the shadows to help him out.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:21.120
Although, something about these underlings&nbsp;
didn't sit right with several moviegoers.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:26.800
During his reign as one of Gotham's most wanted,&nbsp;
the Riddler conjured up quite a following online.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:31.280
As the GCPD investigated his apartment,&nbsp;
they searched his laptop and noted that he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:36.960
had roughly 500 online followers — folks that&nbsp;
have listened to his every word and taken his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:41.840
messages of violence to heart. These are the&nbsp;
ones who showed up in full Riddler garb with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:46.240
every intention of firing upon scared and&nbsp;
helpless people at Gotham Square Garden,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:50.160
who huddled there due to Riddler's flood-inducing&nbsp;
destruction of the city's sea wall.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:56.240
The thing is, all 500 of those followers didn't&nbsp;
actually show up. In fact, the final tally was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:01.600
likely less than 100, and those that have already&nbsp;
gone to see the movie took notice. One user on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:06.560
Reddit's "The Batman" spoiler discussion thread,&nbsp;
poking fun at Riddler's fickle fans, commented,

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:10.480
"Only like 10 people actually&nbsp;
showed up for the big event lol."

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:13.600
This prompted a discussion about&nbsp;
the serial killer's failed attempt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.960
at gathering forces to carry out&nbsp;
his plan. Another Redditor added,

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:21.840
"I liked that, thought it was very realistic. In&nbsp;
fact I'm surprised he got that many to show up."

00:02:21.840 --> 00:02:24.000
And a fellow user posits that,

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:27.840
"Probably only 10 were trained and&nbsp;
willing [to] go through with the plan."

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:30.480
Nevertheless, they were no&nbsp;
match for Batman, Catwoman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:34.560
Jim Gordon, and the rest of the GCPD.&nbsp;
Together, they took down these keyboard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:37.760
warriors-turned-gunmen before they&nbsp;
could really start wreaking havoc.

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:41.680
At the end of the day, it should come as no&nbsp;
surprise that good ultimately triumphed over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:46.400
evil in "The Batman." The Riddler wound up behind&nbsp;
bars, the bulk of his "devoted" followers failed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:51.200
to deliver on their online promises, and Batman&nbsp;
earned his place as a true hero in the eyes of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:55.920
Gotham's residents. Still, as evidenced by the&nbsp;
aforementioned Reddit thread, it appears as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:00.960
though Paul Dano's chilling twist on the Riddler&nbsp;
left a lasting impact on fans. In spite of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:05.440
character's murderous tendencies and obvious&nbsp;
inability to find honest cronies, of course.

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:06.880
A Redditor commented,

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:10.720
"Best part for me was Riddler.&nbsp;
Every scene with him was amazing."

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:14.800
And numerous other folks who checked out "The&nbsp;
Batman" recently echoed similar sentiments.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:20.640
One user called Dano's performance, quote, "creepy&nbsp;
and unsettling as a realistic Riddler should be"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:24.800
and defended his over-the-top mannerisms as&nbsp;
perfectly fitting for this version of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:29.840
famed Batman rogue. In expressing their love for&nbsp;
the overall movie, another user compared Riddler&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:35.280
to the real-life Zodiac Killer. Suffice to say,&nbsp;
the unsettling similarities are hard to ignore.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:40.320
There's no denying that Paul Dano's Riddler was&nbsp;
an excellent foil for Robert Pattinson's Batman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:44.080
and could easily remain a thorn in his&nbsp;
side if "The Batman" lands a sequel or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:48.640
two. Should he manage to escape Arkham and&nbsp;
continue terrorizing Gotham City, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:51.920
he might want to look into&nbsp;
enlisting some better henchmen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:56.640
Perhaps then he could actually succeed at&nbsp;
his evil schemes, but then again, it stands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.640 --> 00:04:01.040
to reason that the Caped Crusader and his allies&nbsp;
would more than give them a run for their money.

